  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Mountain instead of Inspiring Vantage as the 3rd land. Inspiring Vantage enters untapped with 2 or fewer other lands (currently has 2), but next turn as the 4th land it will enter tapped. Mountain always enters untapped. By playing Mountain now and Inspiring Vantage next turn, the Inspiring Vantage will enter tapped, losing a mana on turn 4.",
      "action_taken": "Played Mountain as the 3rd land",
      "better_line": "Play Inspiring Vantage as the 3rd land (enters untapped with only 2 other lands), saving Mountain for next turn when it would still enter untapped. This ensures all lands enter untapped across both turns.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 58,
      "player": "KimiK2 Stoic",
      "decision_index": 49,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Played Sacred Foundry untapped (paying 2 life) before casting Slickshot Show-Off. The correct sequencing is to cast Slickshot Show-Off first using the 2 untapped Mountains ({1}{R}), then play Sacred Foundry tapped for free, saving 2 life unnecessarily spent.",
      "action_taken": "Played Sacred Foundry untapped, paying 2 life, before casting Slickshot Show-Off.",
      "better_line": "Cast Slickshot Show-Off first with the 2 untapped Mountains, then play Sacred Foundry tapped (saving 2 life).",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 67,
      "player": "Grok4F Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 58,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 5 life facing an evasive Slickshot Show-Off (1/2 flying) that can't be blocked by ground creatures, KimiK2 played Charming Prince instead of killing the Slickshot with Burst Lightning. Burst Lightning costs just {R} to deal 2 damage to the 1/2 Slickshot, killing it, and then there's still mana left to cast Charming Prince for the life gain. This leaves the flying threat alive that could easily deal lethal with any pump spell.",
      "action_taken": "Played Inspiring Vantage and cast Charming Prince without removing Slickshot Show-Off.",
      "better_line": "Cast Burst Lightning targeting Slickshot Show-Off (kills it for {R}), then play Inspiring Vantage, then cast Charming Prince choosing gain 3 life. This removes the evasive threat AND develops the board AND gains life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 72,
      "player": "KimiK2 Stoic",
      "decision_index": 63,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Targeting the opponent's face with Burst Lightning instead of Momo allows the opponent to block Slickshot Show-Off with Momo and survive at 3 life. Targeting Momo directly would kill Momo, guarantee Slickshot connects unblocked for 3 flying damage, and leave the opponent at 2 life instead of 3.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted KimiK2 Stoic (opponent at 5 life) with Burst Lightning for 2 damage during combat.",
      "better_line": "Target Momo, Friendly Flier with Burst Lightning to kill it (2 damage to 1/1), ensuring Slickshot Show-Off (3/2 flying after trigger) connects unblocked for 3 damage, leaving opponent at 2 life instead of 3.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 80,
      "player": "Grok4F Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 71,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "KimiK2 Stoic is at 1 life facing a 3/2 Slickshot Show-Off attack. They have Sarkhan, Dragon Ascendant (which should be at least 2/2 or 3/3), Momo, Friendly Flier, and Charming Prince available as blockers. Any of these creatures could block the Slickshot Show-Off and prevent the lethal damage. The player's reasoning even correctly identifies they should block with Sarkhan, but somehow no blocker was actually assigned, resulting in the Slickshot dealing 3 damage and killing them.",
      "action_taken": "Failed to assign any blocker to Slickshot Show-Off, letting it deal 3 lethal damage while at 1 life.",
      "better_line": "Block Slickshot Show-Off with Sarkhan, Dragon Ascendant (or any available creature). Sarkhan as a 3/3 would kill the 3/2 Slickshot and survive, completely neutralizing the attack and keeping KimiK2 alive.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 80,
      "player": "KimiK2 Stoic",
      "decision_index": 73,
    }
  ],
